  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: 23-0001793 Support towards establishment of a Kenya Refugee Evidence Platform and Localisation Agenda (KREPLA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPACT: 23-0001793 This activity seeks to support establishment of a locally-led research and policy advocacy platform on refugee issues in Kenya. The platform will work as a one-stop shop towards evidence generation, synthesis of existing studies and best practices, offer thought leadership and critical reflection on political economy analysis of refugee issues. Periodic multi-stakeholder learning exchanges with government authorities, donors, humanitarian and development actors, academia and refugee researchers will be convened with a view to inform programe adaptation and policy dialogue processes on refugee hosting in Kenya. A jointly developed common research and policy agenda will guide the work of the platform and support towards achievement of durable solutions for refugees and host communities in Kenya. The platform will be managed by a consortium made up of the Regional Durable Solutions Secretariat (ReDSS) &#x2013; as the lead partner; the Refugee-led Research Hub (RLRH) and Maseno University.</narrative>
  </description>
